<h2>What it is for</h2>
<p>Keep the paperwork that belongs with a member of staff (a signed contract, right-to-work evidence, a certificate) on their staff record, in one private place. Care Core stores the files and says who added or removed each one. It does not read them.</p>

<h2>Adding a document</h2>
<p>Open <strong>People → a person → Staff record → Documents</strong>. Choose a file (PDF, Word .docx, PNG or JPEG, up to 10 MB), give it a title, choose what kind it is and, if it runs out, an expiry date. Care Core checks what the file actually is, not what its name says, so a program renamed to end in .pdf is refused. You cannot add documents to your own record unless you are an administrator.</p>

<h2>Who can see them</h2>
<ul>
<li>Managers and administrators can download any document, as a file. Documents are never shown in the browser.</li>
<li>The person can download a document only if you tick <strong>They can see it</strong>. It then appears under <em>My profile</em>. Untick it to take it away again.</li>
<li>Files are kept outside the public part of the website and are only given out after these checks.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Expiry</h2>
<p><strong>Documents to review</strong> (from People or Team leave) lists documents that have expired or expire within 60 days, soonest first. Care Core does not email anyone about them.</p>

<h2>Retention</h2>
<p>How long you keep a leaver’s records is a decision for your organisation. On <strong>Documents to review</strong>, enter a number of years and the page lists people who left longer ago than that and have no current job, with how many documents each holds. It is a list to review: Care Core never deletes anything on its own, and a person’s record in People is never deleted (that is a core rule). To act on it, open the person and remove their documents.</p>

<h2>Subject access requests</h2>
<p>On the Documents fold, <strong>Download everything held about</strong> the person gives a single file (JSON) of what Care Core holds about them: details, address and pay details (decrypted, because they are theirs), employments and changes, team places, registrations, supervisions, appraisals and learning, leave and absence, tasks, a list of their documents and the activity log about them. It says plainly what it does <em>not</em> include: the document files themselves (download them one by one), anything held outside Care Core, and information about other people that may need to be left out before you share it. Making the export is recorded in the activity log.</p>
